### Goal Model Design for Food Delivery and Dish Retrieval in a Hospital Setting

The goal model is structured to handle both food delivery and dish retrieval efficiently, considering the need for flexibility and cooperation between robots and humans.

#### Goals

| Name | Text | Runtime | Goal Type | Relation | Justification |
|------|------|---------|-----------|----------|---------------|
| G1   | Deliver food and retrieve dirty dishes in a hospital setting. | - | Achieve | - | Ensures the desired condition of completing deliveries and retrievals. |
| G2   | Deliver food to inpatient rooms. | - | Achieve | AND with G3 | Both delivery and retrieval are necessary for the mission. |
| G3   | Retrieve dirty dishes from inpatient rooms. | - | Achieve | AND with G2 | Both tasks are essential for the mission's success. |
| G2.1 | Deliver food directly using special manipulation skills. | ; | Perform | OR with G2.2 | Alternative method of delivery. |
| G2.2 | Deliver food for retrieval from the robot's tray. | - | Achieve | OR with G2.1 | Another method for delivering food. |
| G2.2.1 | Query inpatient record for retrieval capability. | - | Query | AND with G2.2.2 | Determines if the inpatient can retrieve food. |
| G2.2.2 | Retrieve food with assistance. | - | Perform | AND with G2.2.1 | Ensures food is retrieved if the inpatient cannot. |
| G2.3 | Track meal retrieval and alert for errors. | ; | Perform | AND with G2 | Ensures correct meals are delivered. |
| G3.1 | Retrieve dishes unassisted. | - | Perform | OR with G3.2 | One method of dish retrieval. |
| G3.2 | Retrieve dishes with cooperation. | - | Perform | OR with G3.1 | Another method for retrieving dishes. |
| G3.2.1 | Retrieve dishes with another robot. | - | Perform | AND with G3.2.2 | Cooperative retrieval with a robot. |
| G3.2.2 | Retrieve dishes with a human. | - | Perform | AND with G3.2.1 | Cooperative retrieval with a human. |
| G3.3 | Query patient's ability to open the door. | - | Query | AND with G3 | Determines if the patient can assist in retrieval. |

#### Tasks

| Name | Text | Relation | Location | Number of Robots | Justification |
|------|------|----------|----------|------------------|---------------|
| AT1  | Move to delivery room. | AND with G2.1 | Kitchen | 1 | Single robot for delivery. |
| AT2  | Deliver meal. | AND with G2.1 | Patient's room | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT3  | Return to kitchen. | AND with G2.1 | Kitchen | 1 | Single robot for return. |
| AT4  | Check inpatient record. | AND with G2.2.1 | Hospital database | 1 | Single robot query. |
| AT5  | Assist with meal retrieval. | AND with G2.2.2 | Patient's room | 1 or more | Ensures assistance if needed. |
| AT6  | Track meal retrieval. | AND with G2.3 | Hospital system | 1 | Monitors retrieval status. |
| AT7  | Alert for wrong meal. | AND with G2.3 | Hospital system | 1 | Ensures correct meals are delivered. |
| AT8  | Move to dish retrieval room. | AND with G3.1 | Patient's room | 1 | Single robot for unassisted retrieval. |
| AT9  | Retrieve dishes. | AND with G3.1 | Patient's room | 1 | Single robot action. |
| AT10 | Return with dishes. | AND with G3.1 | Kitchen | 1 | Single robot for return. |
| AT11 | Cooperate with another robot. | AND with G3.2.1 | Patient's room | 2 | Ensures efficient retrieval. |
| AT12 | Retrieve dishes with human help. | AND with G3.2.2 | Patient's room | 1 | Single robot with human assistance. |
| AT13 | Signal for door opening. | AND with G3.3 | Patient's room | 1 | Ensures door is opened if needed. |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both food delivery and dish retrieval are necessary for the mission's success.

- **G2 -> G2.1, G2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either direct delivery or tray retrieval can be used.

- **G2.2 -> G2.2.1, G2.2.2 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both querying the record and assisting if needed are required for tray retrieval.

- **G2.3 -> AT6, AT7 [AND]**  
  Justification: Both tracking and alerting are necessary for correct meal delivery.

- **G3 -> G3.1, G3.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Either unassisted or cooperative retrieval can be used.

- **G3.2 -> G3.2.1, G3.2.2 [OR]**  
  Justification: Retrieval can be done with another robot or a human.

This goal model ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, with flexibility and cooperation where needed.
